# `pluss::subsp::stats::ts::AdfResult`

Result of `ts::adf_test`.

`AdfResult` carries the statistic and what is needed to read it.

## Fields

| Field | Type | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `stat` | `double` | — | The t-ratio of the lagged level's coefficient. |
| `pvalue` | `double` | — | Probability under the null of a unit root, from the response-surface approximation. |
| `critical` | `double` | — | Critical value at `alpha` for the sample size and model. |
| `reject` | `bool` | — | True when the statistic is below the critical value: the unit root is rejected. |
| `lags` | `std::int64_t` | — | Augmentation lags used. |
| `effective_n` | `std::int64_t` | — | Observations in the test regression. |

## Guidance

The defaults are a sensible starting point; change a field only for the reason its row gives.

## See Also

- [`adf_test`](adf_test.md)

